The goal of this PR is to add a new `fetch` effect that will properly cancel `window.fetch` when the saga running it is cancelled.

## with `fetcher`
```js
import { fetcher } from 'redux-saga/effects';

function* fetchUsers() {
  const result = yield fetcher('/users');
  const data = yield call([result, 'json']);
  console.log(data);
}
```

## with `abortController`
```js
import { abortController } from 'redux-saga/effects';

function* fetchUsers() {
  const { signal } = yield abortController();
  const result = yield call(fetch, '/users', { signal });
  const data = yield call([result, 'json']);
  console.log(data);
}
```

I really like the ergonomics of the `fetch` effect and for the most common case this is what people are going to be using `AbortController` for so I think it's useful as a stand-alone.

I haven't written docs or tests yet because I want us to discuss the API a little more.

Fix `GridInventory#set(x, y, stack)`, `#slot(x, y)` etc methods coordinates being inverted.

Test code : 
```java
ViewableInventory inv = ViewableInventory.builder().type(ContainerTypes.GENERIC_9X6).completeStructure().plugin(plugin).build();
GridInventory grid = inv.query(GridInventory.class).get();

for (int y = 0; y < 9; y++) {
    for (int x = 0; x < 9; x++) {
        grid.set(x, y, ItemStack.builder().itemType(ItemTypes.STONE).add(Keys.CUSTOM_NAME, Component.text("x=" + x + " y=" + y)).build());
    }
}
        
player.openInventory(inv);
```


